  learnt on: A-phase=port2.0.2  B-phase=port1.0.2  A-again=port2.0.2
  exactly one FDB entry at each phase: True
  entry moved A->B->A:                True

VERDICT: PASS -- the MAC moves between ports and never duplicates

NOTE: this exercises MAC MOVEMENT. Sustained MAC THRASH (a MAC flapping fast
enough to trigger thrash protection/logging) is not attempted -- the case
gives no rate or threshold, and the bench has one host NIC per DUT port so
the flap rate is bounded by sequential scapy runs, not by the DUT.
